    <title>Sparse Autoencoders Find Highly Interpretable Features in Language
  Models</title>
    <summary>  One of the roadblocks to a better understanding of neural networks' internals
is \emph{polysemanticity}, where neurons appear to activate in multiple,
semantically distinct contexts &amp; resist interpretation.
</summary>
